# macOS
.DS_Store

# Hektor runtime state (written into installed projects, not the pack)
docs/hektor/.hook-audit.log
docs/hektor/.cursor-hook-payload.log
docs/hektor/observations.jsonl
docs/hektor/memory-proposals.md
docs/hektor/skill-stocktake.json

# Build artifacts from `hektor-triage-kit build`. npm pack writes into the directory
# it runs in, which for the kit is this tracked one — and README tells maintainers to
# run it there. The zip was retired (kernel §7/§12) exactly to stop a stale binary
# being committed and drifting from the source; committing a .tgz instead would just
# trade one stale artifact for another. Build it, install it, throw it away.
# Any kit directory, not only the one that existed when this rule was written: a copy taken
# to work on the next version (kits/flaky-triage-kit-next) falls outside a hardcoded name, so
# the guard install-guard-test.sh enforces stopped covering the very tree being edited — it
# failed there and passed in the original, which reads as a defect in the copy rather than a
# gap in this line.
kits/*/*.tgz

# achilles test scratch
.achilles/
